Q: How to convert a .txt file of 0&#39;s and 1&#39;s to a .bin? A: <p>Normally when we work with bit data. If we have bit counter for count bit is full to buffer or not (not count bits in buffer). it's will make program easier.</p>
<pre class="lang-cpp prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;iostream&gt;
#include &lt;sstream&gt;
#include &lt;cstdint&gt;


int main(int argc, char* argv[]) {

    constexpr auto input = R&quot;(00110010 10 11 011
11110000 10 1   0 0 0  0 0 0 111
0111 001 01 01 0 0 0111 1011)&quot;;//assume to your data in file

    std::istringstream is{ input };// assume to std::ifstream

    std::string str_buf;
    uint8_t bit_buf = 0;//be careful if use write buffer more than 1 byte, data in file will affected by system endian
    int underflow = 8;//counter

    while (is &gt;&gt; str_buf) {
        for (char c: str_buf) {
            switch (c) {
            case '0':
                underflow--;
                break;
            case '1':
                bit_buf |= 1 &lt;&lt; underflow--;
                break;
            default:
                std::cerr &lt;&lt; &quot;skip or do something\n&quot;;
                break;
            }

            if (underflow == 0) {
                /*
                    flush/write to file here and reset bit buf, counter
                */
                underflow = 8; 
                bit_buf = 0;
            }
        }

    }
    if (underflow &lt; 8) {
        /*
            flush/write remain
        */
    }

    return 0;
}
</code></pre>

Q: XSLT to copy elements from source into CDATA section A: <p>Might the following work?:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;xsl:template match=&quot;SOAP-ENV:Body&quot;&gt;
    &lt;xsl:element name=&quot;s:{local-name()}&quot; namespace=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2003/05/soap-envelope&quot;&gt;
        &lt;xsl:element name=&quot;cais:SendMessage&quot; namespace=&quot;http://www.ortec.com/CAIS&quot;&gt;
            &lt;xsl:element name=&quot;cais:message&quot; namespace=&quot;http://www.ortec.com/CAIS&quot;&gt;
                &lt;!-- copy the rest --&gt;
                &lt;xsl:text disable-output-escaping=&quot;yes&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;![CDATA[&lt;/xsl:text&gt;
                &lt;xsl:apply-templates select=&quot;child::node()&quot;/&gt;
                &lt;xsl:text disable-output-escaping=&quot;yes&quot;&gt;]]&amp;gt;&lt;/xsl:text&gt;
            &lt;/xsl:element&gt;
            &lt;xsl:element name=&quot;cais:commandName&quot; namespace=&quot;http://www.ortec.com/CAIS&quot;&gt;Import&lt;/xsl:element&gt;
        &lt;/xsl:element&gt;
    &lt;/xsl:element&gt;
&lt;/xsl:template&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>When I modify the XSLT in this way and run it on your sample input, I get:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;s:Envelope xmlns:s=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2003/05/soap-envelope&quot;&gt;
  &lt;s:Header&gt;&lt;a:Action s:mustUnderstand=&quot;1&quot; xmlns:a=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2005/08/addressing&quot;&gt;http://www.ortec.com/CAIS/IApplicationIntegrationService/SendMessage&lt;/a:Action&gt;&lt;/s:Header&gt;
  &lt;s:Body&gt;&lt;cais:SendMessage xmlns:cais=&quot;http://www.ortec.com/CAIS&quot;&gt;&lt;cais:message&gt;
  &lt;![CDATA[
    &lt;test xmlns:SOAP-ENV=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot;&gt;
      &lt;element1&gt;123&lt;/element1&gt;
      &lt;element2&gt;123&lt;/element2&gt;
    &lt;/test&gt;
  ]]&gt;
  &lt;/cais:message&gt;
  &lt;cais:commandName&gt;Import&lt;/cais:commandName&gt;&lt;/cais:SendMessage&gt;&lt;/s:Body&gt;
&lt;/s:Envelope&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>The namespace declaration is still there, but that shouldn't really matter.</p>
<p>If you really want to get rid of the namespace declaration on <code>&lt;test&gt;</code>, you can replace your identity template with this:</p>
<pre><code>  &lt;xsl:template match=&quot;@* | node()&quot; priority=&quot;-2&quot;&gt;
    &lt;xsl:copy&gt;
      &lt;xsl:apply-templates select=&quot;@*|node()&quot;/&gt;
    &lt;/xsl:copy&gt;
  &lt;/xsl:template&gt;

  &lt;xsl:template match=&quot;*&quot;&gt;
    &lt;xsl:element name=&quot;{name()}&quot;&gt;
      &lt;xsl:apply-templates select=&quot;@* | node()&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;/xsl:element&gt;
  &lt;/xsl:template&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>I've verified that that seems to work.</p>
<p>And just as a side note, if you know the prefix and name of your elements ahead of time, you don't need to use <code>xsl:element</code> or <code>namespace</code> attributes.  If you declare your namespaces in the <code>xsl:stylesheet</code> element:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;xsl:stylesheet version=&quot;2.0&quot; xmlns:xsl=&quot;http://www.w3.org/1999/XSL/Transform&quot; 
                   xmlns:xs=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema&quot; 
                   xmlns:fn=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2005/xpath-functions&quot; 
                   xmlns:SOAP-ENV=&quot;http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/&quot; 
                   xmlns:s=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2003/05/soap-envelope&quot;
                   xmlns:cais=&quot;http://www.ortec.com/CAIS&quot;
                   exclude-result-prefixes=&quot;fn xs SOAP-ENV cais&quot;&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Then you can just do this:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;xsl:template match=&quot;SOAP-ENV:Body&quot;&gt;
    &lt;xsl:element name=&quot;s:{local-name()}&quot;&gt;
        &lt;cais:SendMessage&gt;
            &lt;cais:message&gt;
                &lt;!-- copy the rest --&gt;
                &lt;xsl:text disable-output-escaping=&quot;yes&quot;&gt;&amp;lt;![CDATA[&lt;/xsl:text&gt;
                &lt;xsl:apply-templates select=&quot;child::node()&quot;/&gt;
                &lt;xsl:text disable-output-escaping=&quot;yes&quot;&gt;]]&amp;gt;&lt;/xsl:text&gt;
            &lt;/cais:message&gt;
            &lt;cais:commandName&gt;Import&lt;/cais:commandName&gt;
        &lt;/cais:SendMessage&gt;
    &lt;/xsl:element&gt;
&lt;/xsl:template&gt;
</code></pre>
